---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
import { crisis } from '../lib/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Page
  title="Disclaimer"
  eyebrow="Please read"
  lede="Hausla is here to help you understand and find your way. It is not a substitute for your doctors."
  updated="2026-11-11"
>
  <div class="callout warm">
    <p><strong>In an emergency, don't wait.</strong> Call {crisis.lines.map((l, i) => <>{i > 0 && ' or '}<a href={`tel:${l.tel}`}>{l.number}</a> ({l.name.split(' (')[0]})</>)}, or go to the nearest hospital emergency department.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="not-advice">Information, not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on Hausla is general information for education and support. It is <strong>not medical advice</strong>,
    and it cannot take account of your situation, history or test results. Hausla does not diagnose conditions,
    recommend treatments, or predict how an illness or treatment will turn out.
  </p>
  <p>
    Always talk to a qualified doctor about your health and before starting, stopping or changing any treatment.
    Never ignore professional advice, or delay seeking it, because of something you read here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="review">Review status</h2>
  <p>
    Our medical pages are currently plain-language <strong>summaries of official sources</strong> and have not yet been
    reviewed by a medical professional. Each page says so at the top. See our
    <a href={url('/editorial-policy')}>editorial policy</a> for how content is made.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">Accuracy and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep information correct and current, and every directory entry shows when it was last checked.
    But medical guidance, hospital contacts, scheme rules and costs change, sometimes without notice. Please confirm
    important details, such as eligibility, fees, timings and phone numbers, directly with the hospital, scheme or
    organisation before acting on them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="listings">Listings are not recommendations</h2>
  <p>
    Including a hospital, organisation, helpline, community or online account on Hausla does not mean we endorse it
    or vouch for the quality of its care or advice. No one pays to be listed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="communities">Communities and stories</h2>
  <p>
    Online communities and personal stories can be a real comfort. They reflect individual experiences and offer
    peer support, not professional advice. What helped one person may not be right for another.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to other websites that we believe are useful and trustworthy. We don't control them and aren't responsible
    for their content, availability or privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Found a problem?</h2>
  <p>If you find something inaccurate or unsafe, please <Contact purpose="report" />.</p>
</Page>
